│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ symmetric_collective_mixer                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized line ansatz with a permutation-equivariant, QAOA-style      │
│                          │ collective mixer. The original two RZ layers commute through the CZ layer and are         │
│                          │ therefore partly redundant; the final RZ layer is also invisible to a Z-basis readout in  │
│                          │ the last block. Shared RY/RZ rotations, a complete-graph CZ interaction matching the      │
│                          │ all-pairs feature geometry, and a final shared RX rotation preserve phase sensitivity     │
│                          │ while making every rotation relevant to the readout. Complete-graph CZ and collective     │
│                          │ rotations remove arbitrary endpoint bias from the line topology and align with the mean-Z │
│                          │ readout. Parameter sharing reduces the block from 24 parameters to 3, lowering the full   │
│                          │ model from 146 to 20 parameters, which should improve generalization, parameter           │
│                          │ efficiency, and Adam convergence while retaining nonlinear all-qubit expressivity.        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
