│ patch_name               │ collective_xy_reupload                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This design replaces the independently parameterized hardware-efficient block with a      │
│                          │ permutation-equivariant collective mixer. All qubits share one RY angle and one RX angle  │
│                          │ within each block, matching the symmetry of the 28 pairwise feature couplings and the     │
│                          │ mean-Z readout. The fixed IsingZZ feature map already supplies data-dependent             │
│                          │ entanglement, so additional fixed entanglers are unnecessary.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The two independently parameterized repeats after each upload compose the shared X/Y      │
│                          │ rotations into a flexible collective single-qubit transformation. Using noncommuting X    │
│                          │ and Y axes also converts the uploaded phase information into measurable Z populations,    │
│                          │ while avoiding redundant RZ-heavy layers. The result uses only 2 parameters per block and │
│                          │ 14 total parameters, compared with 146 in the seed, while reducing circuit gate count and │
│                          │ depth and imposing a strong inductive bias intended to improve generalization and         │
│                          │ convergence.                                                                              │
