╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ compact_ry_czring_rz                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Key changes from the current 24-param-per-block ansatz (RY+RZ_pre+CZ_line+RZ_post):       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Removed the pre-CZ RZ layer (8 params eliminated per block): Since blocks are applied  │
│                          │ sequentially, the post-CZ RZ from the previous block followed by the pre-CZ RY of the     │
│                          │ next block already provides an effective RZ-RY rotation pair. This makes the dedicated    │
│                          │ pre-CZ RZ layer redundant.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Upgraded CZ line (7 gates) to CZ ring (8 gates): Added CZ(7,0) to close the ring,      │
│                          │ providing full circular connectivity with a brick-layer pattern (even pairs then odd      │
│                          │ pairs). This slightly improves entanglement structure.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Parameter reduction: 16 params/block × 6 blocks = 96 circuit + 2 readout = 98 total    │
│                          │ (vs 146), a 33% reduction. This significantly improves parameter_efficiency               │
