│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replacing the RY and RZ gates with a full RZ-RY-RZ sequence implements an arbitrary local │
│                          │ single-qubit rotation (U3) via Euler angles. This provides maximum expressiveness per     │
│                          │ qubit within the ansatz before the entangling CZ operations. Additionally, by modifying   │
│                          │ the entanglement map from a line (or disjoint pairs) to a full contiguous ring (i.e.,     │
│                          │ nearest neighbor CZ gates with periodic boundary conditions), entanglement is             │
│                          │ symmetrically distributed across all 8 qubits. This approach quadruples the number of     │
│                          │ trainable Z-rotations relative to the Y-rotations in the block without significantly      │
│                          │ increasing depth.                                                                         │
