│ patch_name               │ pruned_zigzag_rx_ansatz                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate rewrites the entangling block to use a pruned 1D "zig-zag" ladder of CZ    │
│                          │ gates. By eliminating the cyclic (7,0) connection, we slightly lower the gate count and   │
│                          │ depth overhead while preserving full multi-qubit entanglement and connectivity through    │
│                          │ staggered adjacent pairings. Additionally, the trailing rotation layer utilizes RX gates  │
│                          │ instead of RZ gates. Because RX does not commute with the Z-based entanglement of the CZs │
│                          │ and the IsingZZ feature uploads, it forces a stronger basis change that has empirically   │
│                          │ demonstrated faster training convergence and ultimately better test loss in prior trials. │
